.TH "MFD" "1" "" "move\-forward" "Move Forward Manual"
.SH NAME
mfd \- local dashboard of PRs, stacks, local work and Jira tickets that
need attention
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]mfd\f[R] [\f[B]\-c\f[R] \f[I]config\f[R]] [\f[B]\-v\f[R]]
\f[I]command\f[R] [\f[I]args\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A local dashboard of everything in flight: my PRs and what they\(aqre
waiting on, reviews asked of me, PRs my team should look at, local
branches with unpushed or uncommitted work, git stack health, todos and
merge conditions from my work notes, my Jira tickets, mail that needs
me, and whom to ping in Slack about my PRs.
No AI involved: everything is worked out from GitHub, git, Jira, mail,
Slack and the notes.
.PP
It runs a small HTTP server on localhost, refreshes in the background,
and renders HTML.
Browser scripts replace dashboard content after refreshes and actions
while keeping the scroll position, and remember open sections in local
storage.
All state lives in one SQLite database.
.SH SETUP
Requires Python 3.15+, \f[CR]gh\f[R] logged in, and git.
\f[CR]git stack\f[R] is optional (for the \f[CR]git_stack\f[R] plugin).
\f[CR]mfd\f[R] runs the git the environment variable
\f[CR]MOVE_FORWARD_GIT\f[R] names (a path), else the one on PATH, looked
up at its first git command and kept until it exits.
.IP
.EX
python3.15 \(ti/src/move\-forward/dev.py install  \f[I]# .venv, \(gamfd\(ga and its man page, git hooks, \(gamfd init\(ga\f[R]
                                   \f[I]# (on Windows: py \-3.15 dev.py install)\f[R]
mfd serve \-\-open
.EE
.PP
With \c
.UR https://docs.astral.sh/uv/
uv
.UE \c
\ installed, any \f[CR]python3\f[R] from 3.11 on (\f[CR]py\f[R] on
Windows) runs \f[CR]dev.py install\f[R]: uv finds Python 3.15 for
\f[CR].venv\f[R], or downloads it.
Without uv, \f[CR].venv\f[R] is made with the Python that runs
\f[CR]dev.py\f[R], so it has to be 3.15.
.PP
The dashboard listens only on localhost, over plain HTTP.
Browsers treat localhost as a secure context, so nothing it does needs
HTTPS.
.PP
If \f[CR]\(ti/.local/bin\f[R] already has \f[CR]mfd\f[R] from another
clone (or installed another way), \f[CR]dev.py install\f[R] stops and
says so, changing nothing: \f[CR]dev.py install \-\-replace\f[R] takes
it over (except, on Windows, another install\(aqs \f[CR]mfd.exe\f[R],
which you uninstall).
A link to a clone that\(aqs since been deleted it just replaces.
It won\(aqt install a clone in a temporary directory (the system\(aqs,
\f[CR]/tmp\f[R] or \f[CR]/var/tmp\f[R]), which would leave
\f[CR]mfd\f[R] broken once it\(aqs deleted: there, run
\f[CR]python3 dev.py venv\f[R] and
\f[CR]git config core.hooksPath git_hooks\f[R], and use
\f[CR].venv/bin/mfd\f[R] (on Windows,
\f[CR].venv\(rsScripts\(rsmfd.exe\f[R]).
.PP
\f[CR]dev.py install\f[R] ends with \f[CR]mfd init\f[R] when there is no
config yet: it asks for your email, which plugins to set up (github,
git, and git_stack when it\(aqs installed, by default; jira, mail and
slack when you name them), then each chosen plugin\(aqs settings, with a
guess from the machine as the default (the GitHub org of the current
repo\(aqs remote, the teams \f[CR]gh\f[R] says you\(aqre in, your git
email).
Tab completes plugin names, your org\(aqs team slugs and repo paths, and
the org question takes the org\(aqs URL pasted whole
(\f[CR]https://github.com/acme\f[R]).
It writes \f[CR]\(ti/.config/move\-forward/config.toml\f[R] with the
rest of the settings as commented defaults, each with the first sentence
