replaces an existing file.
.PP
The top level of the config says who you are and how the dashboard runs:
\f[CR]email\f[R], \f[CR]port\f[R], \f[CR]db_path\f[R],
\f[CR]db_backups\f[R] and \f[CR]prune_days\f[R].
Each plugin that fetches refreshes on its own schedule, the
\f[CR]refresh_seconds\f[R] in its section (github every 5 minutes, jira
and mail every 15, git and git stack every 30 behind watching their
repos, by default), and sooner when its plugin can tell cheaply that its
tool has something new (each plugin\(aqs page says how).
Loading the page refreshes nothing: the Refresh buttons (a plugin\(aqs,
or the header\(aqs) and an item\(aqs ↻ do.
Everything about a tool is in that tool\(aqs plugin section; see
Plugins.
.PP
\f[CR][people]\f[R] says what the kinds of people I deal with mean:
\f[CR]contact_types\f[R]
(\f[CR]{ customer = 1, partner = 1, vendor = 0 }\f[R]) are the types the
Set type button offers, each with the importance (0 normal, 1 high, 2
critical) it gives items about such a person.
Another type can still be set; it counts as 0.
See People.
.PP
\f[CR][act_now]\f[R] tunes how Act now ranks what the plugins nominate:
\f[CR]size\f[R] (7, the items shown), \f[CR]per_plugin\f[R] (3, the most
one plugin may fill) and \f[CR]weights\f[R] (what each signal adds to an
item\(aqs score: \f[CR]closes = 3\f[R], \f[CR]minutes = 2\f[R],
\f[CR]hour = 1\f[R], \f[CR]waiting = 2\f[R] (plus 1 for each doubling of
the days they\(aqve waited), \f[CR]importance = 3\f[R] per level (high,
critical), and \f[CR]due = 1\f[R] times the due date\(aqs pressure, 0
\f[CR]due_warning_days\f[R] or more ahead and rising to 4 once it\(aqs
past, and \f[CR]blocked = \-4\f[R] for a blocked item).
A blocked item (a ticket with open blockers, an entry blocked on
something) is ranked down, until it has gone
\f[CR]blocked_stale_days\f[R] (3; 0 means never) without a touch: a
ticket\(aqs last update or comment, an entry\(aqs last edit.
Then it\(aqs worth chasing, and ranks as if it weren\(aqt blocked.
A due date starts raising an item \f[CR]due_warning_days\f[R] (7) ahead.
A snooze lasts \f[CR]default_snooze_days\f[R] (1: until tomorrow), or
\f[CR]snooze_days[<kind>]\f[R] for a kind of subject
(\f[CR]snooze_days = { pull_request = 7 }\f[R] snoozes a PR for a week),
or until the item changes, whichever comes first; with Snooze\(aqs
\(dquntil it changes\(dq, only when it changes (or once it\(aqs
\f[CR]prune_days\f[R] old).
A timed snooze ends at local midnight, or at
\f[CR]snooze_until_hour\f[R] (9: nine in the morning) on its last day.
.SH PLUGINS
Each external tool is a plugin, enabled by its section in the config:
leave a section out and the plugin, its panels and its fetching are off.
Plugins learn about each other\(aqs data only through a shared graph of
entities (PRs, tickets, branches, ...), listed in docs/entities.md;
docs/graph.md explains how the graph works, and docs/plugins.md draws
who publishes and reads what; docs/writing\-a\-plugin.md walks through
making one, and docs/plugin_contract.md lists everything a plugin is to
core.
A plugin built on another\(aqs entities needs that plugin\(aqs section
too; the config fails to load without it, saying which (e.g.
\(dq[git_stack] needs [git]\(dq).
.PP
