.PP
Both focus pages take \f[CR]tag\f[R] as \f[CR]/\f[R] does.
.PP
Plugins add pages and buttons of their own, listed on their pages (see
Plugins).
.PP
\f[CR]POST /refresh/subjects\f[R] (JSON,
\f[CR][{\(dqkind\(dq: ..., \(dqid\(dq: ...}]\f[R], at most 50) asks for
those entities to be fetched again, ahead of any refresh that\(aqs due:
a refresh of the plugins that publish them, each narrowed to them where
it can be, recorded as any refresh.
A plugin whose refresh is asked for by name or falls due in the same
round is refreshed as it would have been, given them too.
It answers \f[CR]204 No Content\f[R], or \f[CR]400\f[R] for a body that
isn\(aqt one.
.PP
\f[CR]POST /layout\f[R] (JSON, sent by the page\(aqs drag script) stores
the page\(aqs order:
\f[CR]{\(dqgroups\(dq: [group keys], \(dqpanels\(dq: {group key: [panel keys]}}\f[R].
It answers \f[CR]204 No Content\f[R], or \f[CR]400\f[R] for a body that
isn\(aqt one.
.PP
\f[CR]GET /notifications/stream\f[R] keeps a signed\-in connection open
and sends notifications as server events (\f[CR]data: <JSON list>\f[R]),
with a heartbeat every five seconds.
\f[CR]POST /notifications\f[R] returns the same JSON once for clients
that cannot use the stream.
Both take the events they deliver from the queue.
The page opens the stream in one tab at a time, so open tabs don\(aqt
use up the browser\(aqs few connections to the dashboard.
.PP
A plugin\(aqs pages are served at \f[CR]/<plugin>/<page>\f[R]
(slack\(aqs ping page is \f[CR]/slack/ping\f[R]), and its own page at
\f[CR]/<plugin>\f[R]; core\(aqs paths\(aq first segments
(\f[CR]focus\f[R], \f[CR]settings\f[R], \f[CR]login\f[R],
\f[CR]notifications\f[R], \f[CR]refresh\f[R], \f[CR]layout\f[R],
\f[CR]actions\f[R], the static files) are reserved.
.PP
Forms (POST, \f[CR]application/x\-www\-form\-urlencoded\f[R]).
A plugin\(aqs buttons post to \f[CR]/actions/<plugin>/<action>\f[R]; the
rest are core\(aqs.
Each answers \f[CR]303 See Other\f[R] to \f[CR]/\f[R] (filtered by the
\f[CR]tag\f[R] query parameters the form posted to, as the page\(aqs
forms do), or to the \f[CR]back\f[R] query parameter when it\(aqs a
local path, with its outcome in a short\-lived cookie the next page
shows once (signed, so no other site or app on localhost can show a
notice of its own); an action that fails says
\f[CR]failed: <reason>\f[R], not an error status.
A malformed request gets one: \f[CR]400\f[R], or \f[CR]413\f[R] for a
body over 64 KiB:
