.SH DAILY CLEAN\-UP
Once a day, after a refresh, work finished more than
\f[CR]prune_days\f[R] (90) days ago is cleared: todos done that long ago
are dropped from the notes, an entry goes when every PR it names was
merged or closed and every ticket in its title resolved that long ago
and it has no open todos (an entry with neither is cleared
\f[CR]prune_days\f[R] after it last changed), a PR, ticket or entry on
ice comes off it once its work is over the same way (a stack stays until
it\(aqs reopened), what the notes remembered
(\f[CR]mfd notes remember\f[R]) as happening that long ago is forgotten,
pings that old leave the database, and so do Act now\(aqs snoozes once
over, and its other snoozes and pins that old.
A priority set on work that\(aqs since finished is cleared, and so is a
tag I put on, or took off, a work entry, todo or mail thread that\(aqs
gone.
A plugin\(aqs problem it hasn\(aqt reported for that long is forgotten
(the plugin was taken out of the config, or no longer checks for it).
Reviewer email and Slack id lookups that found none that long ago are
forgotten, to be tried again.
PR and ticket dates come from \f[CR]gh pr view\f[R] and Jira; without
Jira, ticket keys aren\(aqt known as such, so they hold no entry.
.SH HOW IT STORES THINGS
\f[CR]dashboard.db\f[R] holds what each plugin last fetched, in that
plugin\(aqs own tables (kept when a refresh fails, with the error shown
alongside), the notes in the notes plugin\(aqs tables, the page\(aqs
dragged order (core\(aqs \f[CR]layout\f[R]), what you snoozed or pinned
in Act now (core\(aqs \f[CR]act_now_feedback\f[R]), the priorities, tags
(those you put on, and those you took off until their plugin refreshes)
and contact types you set, the sign\-in sessions, the notifications
waiting to be told, what the panels last showed that notifies when new
and the problems the plugins report (core\(aqs too), where pings go and
the pings sent in the slack plugin\(aqs, reviewers\(aq emails in the
github plugin\(aqs (looked up from commits), and the messages mail reads
in its own.
It\(aqs the source of truth for the notes.
A change is saved as it\(aqs made, but an OS crash or power cut (not an
\f[CR]mfd\f[R] crash) can lose the last half minute or so of changes
(notes, snoozes, priorities); the database itself survives.
The server\(aqs token sits next to it, in \f[CR]token\f[R].
The database, its backups and the token are readable by you alone (on
Windows, by their access lists).
.PP
The schema is built by migrations: core and each plugin own a list,
applied in order at start\-up and kept by name in the
\f[CR]migrations\f[R] table, so an older database upgrades in place.
Before the first migration that would change an existing database,
it\(aqs copied to \f[CR]backups/dashboard.db.<UTC time>\f[R] next to it
(with SQLite\(aqs backup API, so the copy is consistent); the newest
\f[CR]db_backups\f[R] (10) copies are kept, and
\f[CR]db_backups = 0\f[R] turns this off.
To roll back, stop the server and copy a backup over
\f[CR]dashboard.db\f[R].
